= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @anti_dem: The anti-democratic parties of the far right and left - the KPD, NSDAP, and DNVP.
- @far_right: The far right - the NSDAP and DNVP.
- @nsdap: The NSDAP alone.
- @kpd: The KPD.
- @socialist: The Socialist parties of the SPD, KPD and the USPD.
- @easy_discard

@anti_dem
on-arrival: enemies = "anti-democratic parties"; center_strength += 5; reformist_strength += 5; left_dissent += 5; workers_kpd -= 2; workers_nsdap -= 2; workers_dnvp -= 2; kpd_relation -= 10

Attacking the far right and left is popular among all of our party except some members of the nationalliberale, who would prefer we keep our options open with the DNVP. 

@far_right
on-arrival: enemies = "far right"; left_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 5; workers_nsdap -= 3; workers_dnvp -= 3;

Attacking the far right is popular among the entire party (except some more right-wing members who would prefer we also go after the KPD). Our bourgeois coalition partners are also skeptical of our lack of commitment to anti-communism.

@nsdap
on-arrival: enemies = "NSDAP"; neorevisionist_strength += 5; nazi_urgency += 1; workers_nsdap -= 4;

[? if nazi_urgency == 0 : The NSDAP is a tiny party right now. ?]

[? if nazi_urgency >= 0 : The Nazis are a threat to weimar democracy, and must be dealt with. ?]

@kpd
on-arrival: enemies = "KPD"; reformist_strength += 5; left_dissent += 8; reformist_dissent -= 5; kpd_relation -= 15; dvp_relation += 5; z_relation += 5; workers_kpd -= 4;

Attacking the KPD is supported by all but the most left-wing socialists, and wins us some measure of approval among the bourgeois parties. However, If we are to reconcile with the KPD, this may not be the best choice.

@socialist
on-arrival: enemies = "Socialists"; nationalliberale_strength += 5; linksliberale_strength -= 5; spd_relations -= 5; dnvp_relations += 5; uspd_relations -= 5; kpd_relations -= 5; new_middle_spd -= 4; new_middle_kpd -= 4; new_middle_uspd -= 4
choose-if: linksliberale_strength >= 10

[? if linksliberal_strength <= 10 : The left in our party would never allow this. ?]

[? if linksliberale_strength >= 10 : Atacking the socialists is supported by the right, especialy the far-right, but alienates us from the SPD who are otherwise one of the most democratic parties. ?]


Atacking the socialists is supported by the right, especialy the far-right, but alienates us from the SPD who are otherwise one of the most democratic parties. 
